stimulus.description:
A student is writing a class TextTools with two static methods that work with a String of words separated by single spaces.
```java
public class TextTools {
    /** Returns the number of words in s. Words are separated by exactly one space; s is not empty and has no leading or trailing space. */
    public static int countWords(String s) { /* part (a) */ }

    /** Returns the longest word in s. If several words have the greatest length, returns the first of them.
     *  Precondition: s is not empty and has no leading or trailing space, and words are separated by exactly one space. */
    public static String longestWord(String s) { /* part (b) */ }
}
```

parts.model_answer:
One correct implementation (ALTON reference answer):
```java
    public static int countWords(String s) {
        int count = 1;
        for (int i = 0; i < s.length(); i++) {
            if (s.substring(i, i + 1).equals(" ")) {
                count++;
            }
        }
        return count;
    }
```

One correct implementation (ALTON reference answer):
```java
    public static String longestWord(String s) {
        String best = "";
        String rest = s;
        while (rest.length() > 0) {
            int sp = rest.indexOf(" ");
            String word;
            if (sp == -1) {
                word = rest;
                rest = "";
            } else {
                word = rest.substring(0, sp);
                rest = rest.substring(sp + 1);
            }
            if (word.length() > best.length()) {
                best = word;
            }
        }
        return best;
    }
```

