stimulus.description:
A weather station stores readings in an ArrayList of Integer values. A class ListStats analyzes them.
```java
import java.util.ArrayList;

public class ListStats {
    /** Returns the average of the positive values in readings, as a double.
     *  Values that are 0 or negative are ignored. Returns 0.0 if readings contains no positive values. */
    public static double averagePositive(ArrayList<Integer> readings) { /* to be written */ }
}
```

parts.model_answer:
One correct implementation (ALTON reference answer):
```java
    public static double averagePositive(ArrayList<Integer> readings) {
        int sum = 0;
        int count = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < readings.size(); i++) {
            if (readings.get(i) > 0) {
                sum += readings.get(i);
                count++;
            }
        }
        if (count == 0) {
            return 0.0;
        }
        return (double) sum / count;
    }
```

