stimulus.description:
A class NameList works with a list of names stored in an ArrayList of String objects.
```java
import java.util.ArrayList;

public class NameList {
    /** Removes from names every String that is equal to an earlier String in names, so that only the first occurrence of each String remains.
     *  The order of the remaining Strings is not changed. */
    public static void removeLaterDuplicates(ArrayList<String> names) { /* to be written */ }
}
```

parts.model_answer:
One correct implementation (ALTON reference answer):
```java
    public static void removeLaterDuplicates(ArrayList<String> names) {
        for (int i = names.size() - 1; i >= 1; i--) {
            String s = names.get(i);
            if (names.indexOf(s) < i) {
                names.remove(i);
            }
        }
    }
```

