stimulus.description:
A class GridTools contains a method that works with a two-dimensional array of integers.
```java
public class GridTools {
    /** Returns a new two-dimensional array with the same dimensions as grid in which every row of grid appears in reverse order.
     *  The array grid is not changed. Precondition: grid has at least one row and every row has the same positive length. */
    public static int[][] flipRows(int[][] grid) { /* to be written */ }
}
```

parts.model_answer:
One correct implementation (ALTON reference answer):
```java
    public static int[][] flipRows(int[][] grid) {
        int[][] result = new int[grid.length][grid[0].length];
        for (int r = 0; r < grid.length; r++) {
            for (int c = 0; c < grid[r].length; c++) {
                result[r][c] = grid[r][grid[r].length - 1 - c];
            }
        }
        return result;
    }
```

